From d9cd719c89b85715063375160c8aec3fb3897286 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:53:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(post): Sinumerik writes work offsets 5/6 as G505/G506

On the 840D the settable zero offsets are G54..G57 then G505..G599;
G58/G59 are axial programmable offsets that select no frame. The post
wrote the engine's generic G58/G59 verbatim, so a setup on offset 5 or
6 ran in the wrong frame or alarmed. frameWord maps the word for the
opening block and for a probe result that sets an offset (frame 6 is
now set and re-selected as G506); a word naming no settable frame is
refused by name. Decision in docs/decisions/934-sinumerik-g505.md.

Fixes #934

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
